@*
    asp-controller + asp-action build the link URL from the ROUTING rules, instead of us typing it.
        <a asp-controller="Products" asp-action="Create">   becomes   <a href="/Products/Create">
        <a asp-controller="Products" asp-action="Index">    becomes   <a href="/">
    (Index on Products is the default route, so MVC writes the shortest URL: "/".)

    Why not just write href="/Products/Create"?
    If the route changes (e.g. to "/shop/products/new"), every hand-typed link breaks silently.
    Tag-helper links are generated from the routes, so they update themselves.
    If asp-controller is left out, the CURRENT controller is used.
*@
<nav>
    <a asp-controller="Products" asp-action="Index">All products</a> |
    <a asp-controller="Products" asp-action="Create">Add product</a>
</nav>
